{:edb/db-before-t 917 :edb/db-after-t 918 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534230 50 #inst "2026-10-06T14:59:00.422Z" 13194139534230 true] [17592186100604 1100 "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" 13194139534230 true] [17592186100604 1100 "Let\n$\\begin{bmatrix}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n2. The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" 13194139534230 false] [17592186100604 1145 "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B$. Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B$, the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = {\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A$. Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A$, the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false." 13194139534230 false] [17592186100604 1145 "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false." 13194139534230 true] [17592186100605 1145 "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B$. Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B$, the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$" 13194139534230 false] [17592186100605 1145 "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$" 13194139534230 true] [17592186100606 1100 "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" 13194139534230 true] [17592186100606 1100 "Let\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA$?" 13194139534230 false] [17592186100606 1145 "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A$. Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A$, the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication.\n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$" 13194139534230 false] [17592186100606 1145 "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$" 13194139534230 true] [17592186100782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282820 13194139534230 true] [17592186100782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282862 13194139534230 true] [17592186100782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282869 13194139534230 true] [17592186100782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282887 13194139534230 true] [17592186100782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282894 13194139534230 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282827 13194139534230 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282834 13194139534230 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282841 13194139534230 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282876 13194139534230 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282901 13194139534230 true] [17592186100784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282848 13194139534230 true] [17592186100784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282855 13194139534230 true] [17592186100784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282882 13194139534230 true] [17592186100784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282908 13194139534230 true] [17592186100784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282915 13194139534230 true] [17592186282820 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282821 13194139534230 true] [17592186282820 1089 "q-129437" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282820 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534230 true] [17592186282820 1100 "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\n- The product $RS$ is well defined\n- The product $RP$ is well defined\n- The product $SP$ is well defined" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282820 1113 #uuid "d34ba736-b5e8-5d98-9c72-ef71550ebac1" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282820 1145 "Notice that $P$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false." 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282822 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282823 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282824 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282825 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282826 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1041 "selection" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282824 13194139534230 true] [17592186282821 1110 #uuid "c4ae3c67-73ab-5957-bc41-4e7d63059951" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282822 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534230 true] [17592186282822 1111 #uuid "30f910bd-709e-5567-9db8-b85b93ad6afe" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282823 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282823 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534230 true] [17592186282823 1111 #uuid "dc322ef8-3226-57fc-b63c-a80ab088c871" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282824 1034 "III only" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282824 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534230 true] [17592186282824 1111 #uuid "f9304ac7-8bb9-54b8-8c7b-7370488ec631" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282825 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282825 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534230 true] [17592186282825 1111 #uuid "435ae3b9-1547-5a37-b2b6-30423833182c" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282826 1034 "II only" 13194139534230 true] [17592186282826 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534230 true] [17592186282826 1111 #uuid "1eeee2b3-94cb-5987-a6f8-2